  <h2>What is Jadau?</h2>
  <p>Jadau is a setting technique, not a type of stone. Craftsmen embed stones &ndash; often Polki diamonds, emeralds, rubies and pearls &ndash; into a gold base using fine gold foil, building up rich, layered designs by hand.</p>

  <h2>Jadau at Vaishnavi Jewels</h2>
  <p>Our Jadau work includes bridal necklaces and chokers, full sets, earrings, maang tikkas and bangles, designed for weddings, receptions and festivals.</p>

  <h2>Made to your occasion</h2>
  <p>Because we manufacture in-house, stone colours, size and design can be adapted to your outfit. Visit us in Surat or book a video call.</p>

  <p>Read more: <a href="/blog/polki-vs-jadau-guide">Polki vs Jadau &ndash; what's the difference?</a></p>
